module whole_model_joint_drive

// Example: WHOLE-MODEL JOINT DRIVE — the parent's cost objective drives the
// CHILD's auto param directly, in one merged solve, instead of the child
// freezing bottom-up first and the parent merely reading the frozen result.
//
// See `docs/prds/v0_6/whole-model-joint-drive-seam.md` (tasks #5188 α,
// #5334 δ, #5189 β) for the design rationale.
//
// # The shape
//
//   RivetedPanel
//     sub rivets = Rivet()                 — Costed, one free auto
//     minimize cost(self.descendants)      — INLINED aggregate (load-bearing)
//
// `Rivet` implements the stdlib `Costed` trait (crates/reify-compiler/stdlib/io.ri),
// which supplies the derived cell
//
//     let line_cost : Money = unit_cost * quantity_produced
//
// `Rivet` must NOT re-declare `line_cost` — that derived cell IS the coupling
// the whole seam exists to drive through.  `cost(self.descendants)` expands to
// `[RivetedPanel.rivets.line_cost].sum`, so the parent's objective reads a cell
// that is itself a function of the child's auto `quantity_produced`.
//
// # Merged vs. frozen — the hand-derived arithmetic
//
// The auto is bracketed by a NON-DEGENERATE box:  1.0 ≤ quantity_produced ≤ 100.0,
// and `unit_cost = 0.50USD`, so `line_cost = 0.50USD × quantity_produced` is
// strictly increasing in the auto over a 99-wide interval.
//
//   MERGED (this file, with the `minimize`):
//     The δ cluster spans {RivetedPanel, Rivet}; the solver minimises
//     `line_cost` over the child's auto, so the argmin sits at the LOWER bound.
//       quantity_produced → 1.0        (nudged marginally off the bound by α's
//                                       Money robustness floor, since the
//                                       objective is dimensionally Money)
//       line_cost         → ≈ 0.50 USD
//
//   FROZEN CASCADE (the same model with the parent's `minimize` removed):
//     No cluster forms, so `Rivet` resolves ALONE, bottom-up, with no user
//     objective.  It still has live inequality constraints, so the solver
//     synthesises a Chebyshev-centre objective (`build_centrality_objective`,
//     crates/reify-constraints/src/solver.rs) and the freeze lands at the BOX
//     CENTRE:
//       quantity_produced → ≈ 50.5      ((1.0 + 100.0) / 2)
//       line_cost         → ≈ 25.25 USD
//     Both figures are the derivation, and both were OBSERVED verbatim by
//     evaluating this model minus the `minimize` (50.499999999999915 /
//     25.249999999999957 USD).
//
// The separation is ~half the box width — roughly 50× in cost.  That gap IS the
// user-observable signal: without the joint drive, the parent's cost objective
// cannot reach the child's auto at all and the design is pinned at the
// arbitrary centre of its feasible box.
//
// Both published assertions are COMPARATIVE (strict inequality + strict
// difference), never an absolute converged value — the numbers above are the
// derivation, not the pins.
//
// Integration test:
//   crates/reify-eval/tests/joint_drive_expansion_boundary.rs (BT-5) asserts
//   (i) the child auto resolves STRICTLY DIFFERENT from its frozen-cascade
//   freeze, and (ii) the merged whole-assembly cost is STRICTLY LESS than the
//   frozen-cascade baseline — with that baseline derived in-test by evaluating
//   this same model minus the `minimize`, not from a recorded constant.
//
// # TRAP — the aggregate MUST stay inlined in the `minimize`
//
// Writing `let subtree_cost : Money = cost(self.descendants)` + `minimize
// subtree_cost` forms NO cluster: δ's C1 rule expands objective TERMS only,
// while the non-auto cell map stores each cell's RAW unexpanded `default_expr`,
// so an unexpanded `cost(self.descendants)` surfaces no `line_cost` read at
// all.  That boundary is pinned executably by
// `objective_must_inline_the_aggregate_to_couple`
// (crates/reify-eval/src/resolve_order.rs).  `examples/cost_subtree_aggregate.ri`
// is exactly that non-coupling `let` shape — do not copy its form here.
//
// # Why auto(free), not strict auto
//
// A strict `auto` triggers the uniqueness re-solve, and a `ConstraintNonUnique`
// error would mask the cost signal this example exists to publish.  Same
// reasoning, and the same house precedent, as `examples/continuous_cost_min.ri`
// — uniqueness is not the concern here, the joint drive is.
//
// # v1 boundary
//
// DEPTH-1 Costed descendants only (see `examples/cost_subtree_aggregate.ri`),
// and one auto — well inside the whole-model cluster dimension cap.

structure def Rivet : Costed {
    param supplier          : String = "Acme Fastener"
    param part_number       : String = "R-4210"
    param unit_cost         : Money  = 0.50USD
    param lead_time         : Time   = 24h

    // The joint-drive target.  Bracketed by a NON-DEGENERATE box so the
    // cost-min argmin (lower bound) and the frozen Chebyshev centre (~50.5)
    // are far apart — that separation is what makes the coupling observable.
    param quantity_produced : Real   = auto(free)
    constraint quantity_produced >= 1.0
    constraint quantity_produced <= 100.0
}

structure RivetedPanel {
    sub rivets = Rivet()

    // INLINED — never behind a `let`.  This is the whole point of the fixture.
    minimize cost(self.descendants)

    // Observational only, for `reify eval` legibility.  Reading the aggregate
    // through a `let` is fine ALONGSIDE the inlined `minimize`; it is only
    // fatal as a REPLACEMENT for it.
    let total_cost : Money = cost(self.descendants)
}
